This module groups protocol-specific helpers for layers 5 to 7 of the OSI
model. Each protocol package is organized inside the {Network} package and
usually provides three kinds of classes:

- A `Message` class for constructing and manipulating protocol-specific
  messages.
- A `Serializer` class implementing the {@module network.serializers}
  interface to convert message objects to and from a byte stream.
- Client and server classes that expose the transport-level API used by the
  higher-level channel abstractions.

The client and server wrappers are split by execution model:

- `Client` and `Server` provide event-based implementations intended for use
  with {Network.Poller} and the event-driven channel layer.
- `AsyncClient` and `AsyncServer` provide coroutine-friendly implementations
  intended for use with {Runtime.Scheduler} and the async channel layer.

This makes it possible to use the same protocol abstraction from either an
event-driven application or a coroutine-based application.
